# OnboardAGV — register a single AGV with the master so MQTT messages from
# this AGV are routed to handlers. Wraps VDA5050Master::onboard_agv.
#
# Single-AGV variant. For onboarding multiple AGVs in one call (e.g. from a
# FleetRoster snapshot), use OnboardAGVBatch.srv — the batch sibling.
#
# Request reuses AGVOnboardSpec: same field set is carried inside
# FleetRoster.msg (DM → master fleet snapshot) and inside OnboardAGVBatch.srv
# batch requests, so a caller can build one entry and dispatch it through
# any of the three surfaces.
#
# **Idempotency**: re-onboarding the same {manufacturer, serial_number}
# returns ALREADY_ONBOARDED without disturbing the existing AGV instance.
# FMS clients can call this safely on every startup or on AGV-pool
# addition.
#
# **What onboarding does master-side**:
#   - Creates an AGV instance with a per-AGV ProtocolAdapter.
#   - Subscribes to the AGV's MQTT topics (state, connection, factsheet,
#     visualization).
#   - Adds the AGV to the master's onboarded list (visible to other services
#     like AssignOrder, GetDeviceStatus, etc.).

AGVOnboardSpec agv
---
# Status enum.
#
# SUCCESS              — AGV successfully onboarded.
# ALREADY_ONBOARDED    — an AGV with this {manufacturer, serial_number}
#                        is already in the master's onboard list.
#                        Idempotent no-op; treat as success.
# INVALID_REQUEST      — empty manufacturer or serial_number.
uint8 SUCCESS=0
uint8 ALREADY_ONBOARDED=1
uint8 INVALID_REQUEST=2
uint8 status

# Echo of request — async-fanout correlation.
string manufacturer
string serial_number
